      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(talk): expose gateway audio to plugins",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw plugins cannot currently drive an avatar from the exact audio produced by an existing Gateway-owned Talk session. Browser integrations are forced either to infer speech timing or create a second provider session, and browser-owned agent consults cannot reliably complete workspace/tool work before returning to the same natural realtime conversation.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a provider-neutral, bounded `runtime.talk.subscribeOutputMedia` surface for exact PCM and lifecycle events from Gateway-owned realtime Talk sessions. It also adds an opt-in `agentConsultOwner: \"gateway\"` mode so the Gateway can run OpenClaw agent/tool work and submit the result back into the same realtime session; the default remains client-owned for compatibility.\n\nThe browser UI and avatar renderer remain in the separate [openclaw-avatar-plugin](https://github.com/RomneyDa/openclaw-avatar-plugin) repository. Direct browser WebRTC is intentionally outside this server-side media surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPlugin authors can render responsive avatars from any matching Gateway Talk session without receiving provider credentials or opening duplicate provider connections. Voice users can keep realtime turn-taking and interruption behavior while requests that need OpenClaw tools or workspace context execute through the Gateway.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Post-rebase focused validation: 5 Vitest shards passed (205 tests total across Talk, Gateway, protocol, plugin SDK, and plugin runtime).\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:scripts` passed.\n- Full `pnpm build` passed on the same patch before the final rebase.\n- Live OpenAI Realtime demo completed Gateway-owned consults through `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`, including real workspace write/read tool calls, then spoke the results in the same session.\n- The companion plugin passes typecheck, build, 17 unit tests, browser smoke tests, and responsive viewport checks at 320x240 and 1600x1000.\n",
        "branch": "feat/talk-avatar-plugin-surface",
